":"argument in favor of or against a measure may authorize in writing any other person or persons to","x":210,"y":834,"w":2070,"h":57},{"text":"sign the rebuttal argument.","x":210,"y":917,"w":567,"h":50},{"text":"The undersigned author(s) of the primary argument hereby authorize(s) the following","x":206,"y":1083,"w":1935,"h":58},{"text":"individual(s) to sign (up to five) the rebuttal argument to the primary argument in favor","x":207,"y":1165,"w":1968,"h":57},{"text":"of against circle one) Measure","x":204,"y":1247,"w":704,"h":52},{"text":"NEW SIGNER(S) (PRINT CLEARLY):","x":205,"y":1404,"w":814,"h":52},{"text":"for the Election to be held on November 3, 2026","x":1153,"y":1246,"w":1070,"h":50},{"text":"(date of election)","x":1915,"y":1313,"w":295,"h":41},{"text":"Name of Rebuttal Argument Signer:","x":204,"y":1539,"w":757,"h":52},{"text":"Name of Rebuttal Argument Signer:","x":202,"y":1697,"w":757,"h":52},{"text":"Name of Rebuttal Argument Signer:","x":201,"y":1856,"w":758,"h":51},{"text":"Name of Rebuttal Argument Signer:","x":199,"y":2014,"w":758,"h":52},{"text":"Name of Rebuttal Argument Signer:","x":197,"y":2172,"w":758,"h":52},{"text":"Abigail Korman","x":1004,"y":1519,"w":325,"h":47},{"text":"Jill Ohline","x":1004,"y":1677,"w":207,"h":38},{"text":"k (a \\ldlQnfl","x":1038,"y":2119,"w":423,"h":87},{"text":"(The new signers listed here must sign the Ballot Measure Rebuttal Argument Submission","x":196,"y":2306,"w":2056,"h":58},{"text":"Form)","x":193,"y":2362,"w":135,"h":49},{"text":"NAME(S) & SIGNATURE(S) OF THE PRIMARY ARGUMENT AUTHOR(S):","x":193,"y":2473,"w":1626,"h":58},{"text":"Amelia Garibay Magallån","x":190,"y":2555,"w":539,"h":50},{"text":"Printed Name and Signature ot Author","x":191,"y":2638,"w":817,"h":50},{"text":"Martha Louise Beetley","x":192,"y":2722,"w":478,"h":50},{"text":"Printed Name and Signatuue","x":189,"y":2804,"w":608,"h":51},{"text":"date","x":1978,"y":2642,"w":97,"h":46},{"text":"D te","x":1977,"y":2816,"w":97,"h":37},{"text":"40 Tower Road, San Mateo, CA 94402","x":860,"y":2912,"w":750,"h":44},{"text":"P 650.312.5222 F 650.312.5348 email registrar@smcacre.gov web www.smcacre.gov","x":372,"y":2962,"w":1726,"h":52}]},{"page":6,"width":2448,"height":3168,"lines":[{"text":"Rebuttal to Argument Against Measure E","x":794,"y":266,"w":877,"h":50},{"text":"It's unfortunate our City Council is defending the interests of corporate landlords instead","x":302,"y":387,"w":1850,"h":54},{"text":"of responding to the needs of Bedwood City residents.","x":298,"y":451,"w":1148,"h":51},{"text":"We've spent the past decade pleading with the Redwood City Council to address the","x":298,"y":578,"w":1788,"h":54},{"text":"affordability crisis. But they've chosen not to pass meaningful protections.","x":298,"y":641,"w":1547,"h":54},{"text":"The facts are:","x":296,"y":769,"w":288,"h":39},{"text":"MeasureS will keep 6,300+ apartments affordable for Redwood City families and","x":297,"y":897,"w":1713,"h":53},{"text":"increase housing stability for 40,000 neighbors.","x":296,"y":960,"w":995,"h":52},{"text":"Measure E will NOT cost Redwood City taxpayers anything, as it will be funded by a","x":295,"y":1087,"w":1776,"h":55},{"text":"small per-unit fee on landlords. Measyre E prohibits use of the general fund for its","x":294,"y":1151,"w":1724,"h":54},{"text":"ongoing costs, so why would the City Council raise taxes or cut city services? Corporate","x":292,"y":1215,"w":1863,"h":55},{"text":"landlords, who own most of our rental housing, will pay the largest share of the fees.","x":293,"y":1279,"w":1779,"h":53},{"text":"This works in many other California cities, and it will work for us.","x":290,"y":1342,"w":1354,"h":49},{"text":"Measure E regulates landlords — NOT ordinary homeowners. And small landlords who","x":291,"y":1469,"w":1845,"h":52},{"text":"rent out single-family homes are exempt from rent control under state law.","x":290,"y":1533,"w":1562,"h":50},{"text":"Measure E will NOT impact building affordable housing. State law exempts all units built","x":290,"y":1659,"w":1862,"h":54},{"text":"after 1995 from rent control, meaning there's no impact on building any new housing.","x":288,"y":1722,"w":1797,"h":56},{"text":"Like any landlord, nonprofits that own the few subsidized apartments built before 1995","x":288,"y":1850,"w":1824,"h":53},{"text":"can petition for a higher rent increase if needed.","x":286,"y":1914,"w":1014,"h":48},{"text":"Don't be fooled. Corporate landlords and real estate trusts have bought up 87% of","x":286,"y":2040,"w":1741,"h":55},{"text":"apartments in Redwood City. They are spending big money to defeat Measure E to","x":284,"y":2104,"w":1761,"h":53},{"text":"protect their profits, not to \"protect affordable housing.\"","x":284,"y":2168,"w":1157,"h":51},{"text":"Vote YES on Measure E: Keep Redwood City affordable.","x":281,"y":2294,"w":1211,"h":52},{"text":"Jill Ohline, Small Landlord","x":280,"y":2474,"w":554,"h":44},{"text":"Geogina Castaneda, Affordable Housing Resident","x":280,"y":2537,"w":1067,"h":52},{"text":"Maria Garcia, Homeowner","x":280,"y":2601,"w":565,"h":44},{"text":"Abigail Korman, teacher","x":277,"y":2664,"w":516,"h":47},{"text":"RECEIVED","x":1778,"y":2226,"w":304,"h":56},{"text":"AUG 18 2026","x":1808,"y":2378,"w":259,"h":46},{"text":"City of Redwood Vity","x":1774,"y":2465,"w":308,"h":41},{"text":"City Clerk","x":1856,"y":2524,"w":142,"h":32},{"text":"8","x":2255,"y":455,"w":39,"h":39},{"text":"IO","x":2245,"y":655,"w":56,"h":39},{"text":"10","x":2230,"y":905,"w":55,"h":42},{"text":"(3","x":2238,"y":1659,"w":65,"h":44},{"text":"9","x":2245,"y":1908,"w":46,"h":42},{"text":"14","x":2231,"y":2021,"w":57,"h":65},{"text":"8","x":2260,"y":2170,"w":40,"h":54},{"text":"7","x":2263,"y":2284,"w":36,"h":59},{"text":"228","x":2262,"y":2417,"w":123,"h":63},{"text":"Kyla Valenti, Benefits Analyst II, County of San Mateo (signed in her individual capacity","x":279,"y":2727,"w":1851,"h":56},{"text":"only)","x":277,"y":2792,"w":103,"h":47}]}